{"path":"std/thread/index.html","title":"Module thread","description":"Native threads.","body":{"type":"document","children":[{"type":"anchor","id":"main-content"},{"type":"heading","level":1,"id":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Module thread"}]},{"type":"text","value":"1.0.0 · "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/src/std/thread/mod.rs.html#1-268","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Source"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Native threads."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"id":"the-threading-model","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The threading model"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"An executing Rust program consists of a collection of native OS threads, each with their own stack and local state. Threads can be named, and provide some built-in support for low-level synchronization."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Communication between threads can be done through "},{"type":"link","href":"std/sync/mpsc/index.html","title":"mod std::sync::mpsc","children":[{"type":"text","value":"channels"}]},{"type":"text","value":", Rust’s message-passing types, along with "},{"type":"link","href":"std/sync/index.html","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"other forms of thread synchronization"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and shared-memory data structures. In particular, types that are guaranteed to be threadsafe are easily shared between threads using the atomically-reference-counted container, "},{"type":"link","href":"std/sync/struct.Arc.html","title":"struct std::sync::Arc","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"Arc"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Fatal logic errors in Rust cause "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"thread panic"}]},{"type":"text","value":", during which a thread will unwind the stack, running destructors and freeing owned resources. While not meant as a ‘try/catch’ mechanism, panics in Rust can nonetheless be caught (unless compiling with "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"panic=abort"},{"type":"text","value":") with "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/panic/fn.catch_unwind.html","title":null,"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"catch_unwind"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and recovered from, or alternatively be resumed with "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/panic/fn.resume_unwind.html","title":null,"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"resume_unwind"}]},{"type":"text","value":". If the panic is not caught the thread will exit, but the panic may optionally be detected from a different thread with "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/thread/struct.JoinHandle.html#method.join","title":"method std::thread::JoinHandle::join","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"join"}]},{"type":"text","value":". If the main thread panics without the panic being caught, the application will exit with a non-zero exit code."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When the main thread of a Rust program terminates, the entire program shuts down, even if other threads are still running. However, this module provides convenient facilities for automatically waiting for the termination of a thread (i.e., join)."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"id":"spawning-a-thread","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Spawning a thread"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A new thread can be spawned using the "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/thread/fn.spawn.html","title":"fn std::thread::spawn","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"thread::spawn"}]},{"type":"text","value":" function:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":null,"code":"use std::thread;\n\nthread::spawn(move || {\n    // some work here\n});"},{"type":"link","href":"https://play.rust-lang.org/?code=%23!%5Ballow(unused)%5D%0Afn+main()+%7B%0A++++use+std::thread;%0A++++%0A++++thread::spawn(move+%7C%7C+%7B%0A++++++++//+some+work+here%0A++++%7D);%0A%7D&edition=2024","title":"Run code","children":[]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In this example, the spawned thread is “detached,” which means that there is no way for the program to learn when the spawned thread completes or otherwise terminates."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To learn when a thread completes, it is necessary to capture the "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/thread/struct.JoinHandle.html","title":"struct std::thread::JoinHandle","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"JoinHandle"}]},{"type":"text","value":" object that is returned by the call to "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/thread/fn.spawn.html","title":"fn std::thread::spawn","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"spawn"}]},{"type":"text","value":", which provides a "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"join"},{"type":"text","value":" method that allows the caller to wait for the completion of the spawned thread:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":null,"code":"use std::thread;\n\nlet thread_join_handle = thread::spawn(move || {\n    // some work here\n});\n// some work here\nlet res = thread_join_handle.join();"},{"type":"link","href":"https://play.rust-lang.org/?code=%23!%5Ballow(unused)%5D%0Afn+main()+%7B%0A++++use+std::thread;%0A++++%0A++++let+thread_join_handle+=+thread::spawn(move+%7C%7C+%7B%0A++++++++//+some+work+here%0A++++%7D);%0A++++//+some+work+here%0A++++let+res+=+thread_join_handle.join();%0A%7D&edition=2024","title":"Run code","children":[]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/thread/struct.JoinHandle.html#method.join","title":"method std::thread::JoinHandle::join","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"join"}]},{"type":"text","value":" method returns a "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/thread/type.Result.html","title":"type std::thread::Result","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"thread::Result"}]},{"type":"text","value":" containing "},{"type":"link","href":"std/result/enum.Result.html#variant.Ok","title":"variant std::result::Result::Ok","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"Ok"}]},{"type":"text","value":" of the final value produced by the spawned thread, or "},{"type":"link","href":"std/result/enum.Result.html#variant.Err","title":"variant std::result::Result::Err","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"Err"}]},{"type":"text","value":" of the value given to a call to "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/macro.panic.html","title":"macro std::panic","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"panic!"}]},{"type":"text","value":" if the thread panicked."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Note that there is no parent/child relationship between a thread that spawns a new thread and the thread being spawned. In particular, the spawned thread may or may not outlive the spawning thread, unless the spawning thread is the main thread."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"id":"configuring-threads","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Configuring threads"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A new thread can be configured before it is spawned via the "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/thread/struct.Builder.html","title":"struct std::thread::Builder","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"Builder"}]},{"type":"text","value":" type, which currently allows you to set the name and stack size for the thread:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":null,"code":"use std::thread;\n\nthread::Builder::new().name(\"thread1\".to_string()).spawn(move || {\n    println!(\"Hello, world!\");\n});"},{"type":"link","href":"https://play.rust-lang.org/?code=%23!%5Ballow(unused)%5D%0A%23!%5Ballow(unused_must_use)%5D%0A%0Afn+main()+%7B%0A++++use+std::thread;%0A++++%0A++++thread::Builder::new().name(%22thread1%22.to_string()).spawn(move+%7C%7C+%7B%0A++++++++println!(%22Hello,+world!%22);%0A++++%7D);%0A%7D&edition=2024","title":"Run code","children":[]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"id":"the-thread-type","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"Thread"},{"type":"text","value":" type"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Threads are represented via the "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/thread/struct.Thread.html","title":"struct std::thread::Thread","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"Thread"}]},{"type":"text","value":" type, which you can get in one of two ways:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"start":null,"items":[{"children":[{"type":"text","value":"By spawning a new thread, e.g., using the "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/thread/fn.spawn.html","title":"fn std::thread::spawn","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"thread::spawn"}]},{"type":"text","value":" function, and calling "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/thread/struct.JoinHandle.html#method.thread","title":"method std::thread::JoinHandle::thread","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"thread"}]},{"type":"text","value":" on the "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/thread/struct.JoinHandle.html","title":"struct std::thread::JoinHandle","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"JoinHandle"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"children":[{"type":"text","value":"By requesting the current thread, using the "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/thread/fn.current.html","title":"fn std::thread::current","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"thread::current"}]},{"type":"text","value":" function."}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/thread/fn.current.html","title":"fn std::thread::current","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"thread::current"}]},{"type":"text","value":" function is available even for threads not spawned by the APIs of this module."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"id":"thread-local-storage","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Thread-local storage"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This module also provides an implementation of thread-local storage for Rust programs. Thread-local storage is a method of storing data into a global variable that each thread in the program will have its own copy of. Threads do not share this data, so accesses do not need to be synchronized."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A thread-local key owns the value it contains and will destroy the value when the thread exits. It is created with the "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/macro.thread_local.html","title":"macro std::thread_local","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"thread_local!"}]},{"type":"text","value":" macro and can contain any value that is "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"'static"},{"type":"text","value":" (no borrowed pointers). It provides an accessor function, "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/thread/struct.LocalKey.html#method.with","title":"method std::thread::LocalKey::with","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"with"}]},{"type":"text","value":", that yields a shared reference to the value to the specified closure. Thread-local keys allow only shared access to values, as there would be no way to guarantee uniqueness if mutable borrows were allowed. Most values will want to make use of some form of "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"interior mutability"}]},{"type":"text","value":" through the "},{"type":"link","href":"std/cell/struct.Cell.html","title":"struct std::cell::Cell","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"Cell"}]},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"link","href":"std/cell/struct.RefCell.html","title":"struct std::cell::RefCell","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"RefCell"}]},{"type":"text","value":" types."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"id":"naming-threads","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Naming threads"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Threads are able to have associated names for identification purposes. By default, spawned threads are unnamed. To specify a name for a thread, build the thread with "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/thread/struct.Builder.html","title":"struct std::thread::Builder","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"Builder"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and pass the desired thread name to "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/thread/struct.Builder.html#method.name","title":"method std::thread::Builder::name","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"Builder::name"}]},{"type":"text","value":". To retrieve the thread name from within the thread, use "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/thread/struct.Thread.html#method.name","title":"method std::thread::Thread::name","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"Thread::name"}]},{"type":"text","value":". A couple of examples where the name of a thread gets used:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"start":null,"items":[{"children":[{"type":"text","value":"If a panic occurs in a named thread, the thread name will be printed in the panic message."}]},{"children":[{"type":"text","value":"The thread name is provided to the OS where applicable (e.g., "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"pthread_setname_np"},{"type":"text","value":" in unix-like platforms)."}]}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"id":"stack-size","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Stack size"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The default stack size is platform-dependent and subject to change. Currently, it is 2 MiB on all Tier-1 platforms."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"There are two ways to manually specify the stack size for spawned threads:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"start":null,"items":[{"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Build the thread with "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/thread/struct.Builder.html","title":"struct std::thread::Builder","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"Builder"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and pass the desired stack size to "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/thread/struct.Builder.html#method.stack_size","title":"method std::thread::Builder::stack_size","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"Builder::stack_size"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Set the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"RUST_MIN_STACK"},{"type":"text","value":" environment variable to an integer representing the desired stack size (in bytes). Note that setting "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/thread/struct.Builder.html#method.stack_size","title":"method std::thread::Builder::stack_size","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"Builder::stack_size"}]},{"type":"text","value":" will override this. Be aware that changes to "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"RUST_MIN_STACK"},{"type":"text","value":" may be ignored after program start."}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Note that the stack size of the main thread is "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"not"}]},{"type":"text","value":" determined by Rust."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":"structs","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Structs"}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/thread/struct.AccessError.html","title":"struct std::thread::AccessError","children":[{"type":"text","value":"AccessError"}]}],"definition":[{"type":"text","value":"An error returned by "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/thread/struct.LocalKey.html#method.try_with","title":null,"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"LocalKey::try_with"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/thread/struct.Builder.html","title":"struct std::thread::Builder","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Builder"}]}],"definition":[{"type":"text","value":"Thread factory, which can be used in order to configure the properties of a new thread."}]},{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/thread/struct.JoinHandle.html","title":"struct std::thread::JoinHandle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"JoinHandle"}]}],"definition":[{"type":"text","value":"An owned permission to join on a thread (block on its termination)."}]},{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/thread/struct.LocalKey.html","title":"struct std::thread::LocalKey","children":[{"type":"text","value":"LocalKey"}]}],"definition":[{"type":"text","value":"A thread local storage (TLS) key which owns its contents."}]},{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/thread/struct.Scope.html","title":"struct std::thread::Scope","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Scope"}]}],"definition":[{"type":"text","value":"A scope to spawn scoped threads in."}]},{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/thread/struct.ScopedJoinHandle.html","title":"struct std::thread::ScopedJoinHandle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ScopedJoinHandle"}]}],"definition":[{"type":"text","value":"An owned permission to join on a scoped thread (block on its termination)."}]},{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/thread/struct.Thread.html","title":"struct std::thread::Thread","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Thread"}]}],"definition":[{"type":"text","value":"A handle to a thread."}]},{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/thread/struct.ThreadId.html","title":"struct std::thread::ThreadId","children":[{"type":"text","value":"ThreadId"}]}],"definition":[{"type":"text","value":"A unique identifier for a running thread."}]}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":"functions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Functions"}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/thread/fn.available_parallelism.html","title":"fn std::thread::available_parallelism","children":[{"type":"text","value":"available_parallelism"}]}],"definition":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns an estimate of the default amount of parallelism a program should use."}]},{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/thread/fn.current.html","title":"fn std::thread::current","children":[{"type":"text","value":"current"}]}],"definition":[{"type":"text","value":"Gets a handle to the thread that invokes it."}]},{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/thread/fn.panicking.html","title":"fn std::thread::panicking","children":[{"type":"text","value":"panicking"}]}],"definition":[{"type":"text","value":"Determines whether the current thread is panicking."}]},{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/thread/fn.park.html","title":"fn std::thread::park","children":[{"type":"text","value":"park"}]}],"definition":[{"type":"text","value":"Blocks unless or until the current thread’s token is made available."}]},{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/thread/fn.park_timeout.html","title":"fn std::thread::park_timeout","children":[{"type":"text","value":"park_timeout"}]}],"definition":[{"type":"text","value":"Blocks unless or until the current thread’s token is made available or the specified duration has been reached (may wake spuriously)."}]},{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/thread/fn.park_timeout_ms.html","title":"fn std::thread::park_timeout_ms","children":[{"type":"text","value":"park_timeout_ms"}]},{"type":"text","value":"Deprecated"}],"definition":[{"type":"text","value":"Uses "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/thread/fn.park_timeout.html","title":"fn std::thread::park_timeout","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"park_timeout"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/thread/fn.scope.html","title":"fn std::thread::scope","children":[{"type":"text","value":"scope"}]}],"definition":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates a scope for spawning scoped threads."}]},{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/thread/fn.sleep.html","title":"fn std::thread::sleep","children":[{"type":"text","value":"sleep"}]}],"definition":[{"type":"text","value":"Puts the current thread to sleep for at least the specified amount of time."}]},{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/thread/fn.sleep_ms.html","title":"fn std::thread::sleep_ms","children":[{"type":"text","value":"sleep_ms"}]},{"type":"text","value":"Deprecated"}],"definition":[{"type":"text","value":"Uses "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/thread/fn.sleep.html","title":"fn std::thread::sleep","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"sleep"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/thread/fn.spawn.html","title":"fn std::thread::spawn","children":[{"type":"text","value":"spawn"}]}],"definition":[{"type":"text","value":"Spawns a new thread, returning a "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/thread/struct.JoinHandle.html","title":"struct std::thread::JoinHandle","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"JoinHandle"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for it."}]},{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/thread/fn.yield_now.html","title":"fn std::thread::yield_now","children":[{"type":"text","value":"yield_now"}]}],"definition":[{"type":"text","value":"Cooperatively gives up a timeslice to the OS scheduler."}]},{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/thread/fn.add_spawn_hook.html","title":"fn std::thread::add_spawn_hook","children":[{"type":"text","value":"add_spawn_hook"}]},{"type":"text","value":"Experimental"}],"definition":[{"type":"text","value":"Registers a function to run for every newly thread spawned."}]},{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/thread/fn.current_id.html","title":"fn std::thread::current_id","children":[{"type":"text","value":"current_id"}]},{"type":"text","value":"Experimental"}],"definition":[{"type":"text","value":"Gets the unique identifier of the thread which invokes it."}]},{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/thread/fn.sleep_until.html","title":"fn std::thread::sleep_until","children":[{"type":"text","value":"sleep_until"}]},{"type":"text","value":"Experimental"}],"definition":[{"type":"text","value":"Puts the current thread to sleep until the specified deadline has passed."}]}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":"types","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Aliases"}]},{"type":"definition_list","items":[{"id":null,"term":[{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/thread/type.Result.html","title":"type std::thread::Result","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Result"}]}],"definition":[{"type":"text","value":"A specialized "},{"type":"link","href":"std/result/enum.Result.html","title":"enum std::result::Result","children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"Result"}]},{"type":"text","value":" type for threads."}]}]}]}}
